{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1452151-v20da-does-a-strength-based-difficulty-penalty-apply-to-damage-rolls","id":1452151,"title":"[V20DA] Does a Strength-Based Difficulty Penalty Apply to Damage Rolls?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-14T06:09:37-07:00","id":1452151,"title":"[V20DA] Does a Strength-Based Difficulty Penalty Apply to Damage Rolls?","content":"I was reading over the rules for V20DA Temporis for an upcoming game and I noticed that Leaden Moment reads...<br /> &quot;... apply any successes scored against them to the difficulty of any actions involving Dexterity, Wits and Strength.&quot;<br /> When using this against a target attacking with a melee weapon, does this difficulty increase apply to the attack roll <i>and </i>the damage roll or <i>just</i> the attack roll, with the damage rolling against difficulty 6 as normal? This kind of strength difficulty modifier comes up now and then in WoD and I've always been a little vague on if they apply to both rolls.<br /> <br /> On a similar note, does anyone with experience with the discipline prefer the V20 or V20DA version of Temporis? The V20 version feels a little more balanced but I'm looking for a second opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26893-geesuv","name":"Geesuv","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T08:03:03-07:00","id":1452164,"title":"","content":"In DAV20? No. Damage dice pools are divided by successes rolled, as per the statement earlier in the paragraph -- this refers simply to &quot;targets&quot;, meaning this is a non-specific effect of the discipline power and applies universally. Determining damage isn't an action, it's an additional resolution step to an action already rolled (the attack) meaning the additional effect of difficulty penalties to <i>actions</i> don't apply.<br /> <br /> So, let's say I'm playing a Gangrel with Strength 4, Dex 3, Brawl 5, and feral claws out, attacking a Trujah who uses this power on my character and scores a single success. My attack dice pool is 8 (as per usual), and I'm rolling at difficulty 7 (+1 difficulty due to the Temporis effect). Statistically I'm most likely to score three successes, so we'll go with that.<br /> <br /> That gives me two overage, so my initial damage pool is seven (4 Strength, 2 overage, 1 claws). That gets halved due to the power effect, so the final damage pool to roll is four.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 06-14-2021, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}